# Section Development Standards

**Source of truth:** for current sections / section schema syntax/APIs query `shopify-dev-mcp` (`learn_shopify_api` → `search_docs_chunks`). This file covers only Foundation-specific conventions.

## Core Sections Pattern

**Core Sections** are prefixed `core-` (e.g. `sections/core-section.liquid`). They ingest pattern-library configuration and work with any combination of core or non-core global blocks. Modify them directly when needed, but when pulling updates from the foundation repo, manually sync changes to `sections/core-*.liquid`.

## Foundation Conventions

- Translation keys use the `t:names.*` and `t:settings.*` namespaces (e.g. `"name": "t:names.section_name"`, `"label": "t:settings.padding"`) — never inline English in schema strings.
- Scope padding via inline `--section-padding-*` CSS variables on the section element, consumed by `{% stylesheet %}`:
  ```liquid
  style='
    --section-padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px;
    --section-padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;
  '
  ```
- Eager-load above-the-fold media for LCP: when `section.index < 3`, set `loading='eager'` + `fetchpriority='high'`; otherwise `loading='lazy'` + `fetchpriority='auto'`.

See [snippets.mdc](snippets.mdc) for the `@`-prefixed utility snippets these sections render.
